# DMV Question Bank - Homepage Sections & Structure

## Goal

Create a **professional, trustworthy, high-conversion homepage** for an EdTech DMV test-prep website. Features are already complete; this document focuses **only on structure, layout, and content sections**.

---

## 1. Flash Offer Banner (Conditional)

**Purpose**: Promote limited-time discounts without harming trust or usability.

**Placement**:

* Very top of the page
* Above the navigation bar

**Guidelines**:

* Slim height (32–40px)
* Single-line message
* High contrast but not aggressive
* Dismissible (❌)
* Only visible when an offer is active

**Example Copy**:

> 🎉 Holiday Sale — 50% off Premium. Ends in 24 hours →

---

## 2. Navigation Bar (Sticky)

**Left**:

* Logo
* "DMV Question Bank" title

**Right (Primary CTA)**:

* Premium Login (if the user is not logged in)
* Other buttons - dashboard, profile, logout, etc (if user is logged in)

**Notes**:

* Sticky on scroll

---

## 3. Hero / Introduction Section

**Purpose**: Immediately communicate value and reduce anxiety.

### Layout

* Left: Text + CTA
* Right: Visual (preferably product UI screenshot over stock photo)

### Content

**Headline**:

> Pass Your California DMV Permit Test on the First Try

**Subheadline**:

> Real DMV-style questions, smart practice, and full-length mock tests — updated for 2025.

**Key Highlights**:

* Exact DMV-style questions
* Chapter-wise practice + mock tests
* 98% student pass rate

**CTA Area**:

* State selector button (when clicked it should open a multi-column dialog box to choose a state)
* Primary CTA: **Practice for Free Now**

**Visual**:

* Product UI screenshot (questions, progress, mock test) OR
* Smiling student holding a license (secondary preference)

---

## 4. Trust & Credibility Section

**Purpose**: Build legitimacy early and reduce hesitation.

**Layout**:

* 4–5 stat cards in a horizontal row

**Suggested Stats**:

* Updated for 2025
* 98% pass rate
* 1,000+ students helped
* Based on official CA DMV handbook
* 4.8 average rating

---

## 5. How It Works (Critical Section)

**Purpose**: Make the journey feel simple and achievable.

**3-Step Layout**:

1. Practice real DMV-style questions
2. Take full-length mock tests
3. Read the 15-min revision guide before the exam

**Design**:

* Icons + short captions
* Minimal text

---

## 6. Testimonials Section

**Purpose**: Social proof and confidence building.

**Title**:

> They Passed. You’re Next.

**Subtext**:

> Join 1,000+ students who passed their DMV permit test with us.

**Rating Display**:

* ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ 4.8 average rating

**Testimonials Layout**:

* Horizontally scrollable cards
* Each card includes:

  * Small circular photo
  * Name (and optional location)
  * 1–2 sentence testimonial

**Design Notes**:

* Uniform card height
* Clean layout, soft shadows

---

## 7. Pass Guarantee Section

**Purpose**: Remove risk and increase conversions.

**Headline**:

> Pass Guarantee. Zero Risk.

**Copy**:
If you don’t pass your official DMV test after purchasing our Premium package, simply send us a screenshot of the email showing your test failure and we’ll instantly refund the full amount. No questions asked.

**Design**:

* Highlighted band or card
* Shield or checkmark icon

**CTA**:

> Learn more →

---

## 8. Premium Value / Pricing Preview

**Purpose**: Prepare users for conversion without hard selling.

**Title**:

> Everything You Need to Pass

**Bullets**:

* Unlimited practice questions
* Full-length mock tests
* Detailed explanations
* Pass guarantee

**CTA**:

> View Premium Plans →

---

## 9. FAQ Section

**Purpose**: Address objections and common concerns.

**Title**:

> Got Questions? We’ve Got Answers.

**Guidelines**:

* 6–8 questions max
* Accordion layout

**Suggested Topics**:

* Is this based on official DMV questions?
* How similar are the questions to the real test?
* What if I fail the DMV test?
* Is this California-only?
* How long should I study?

---

## 10. Footer

**Content Areas**:

* Product links
* Resources
* Legal (Terms, Privacy Policy)
* Social media (Facebook, Instagram)

